{"amendments":[{"body":"Fix `SimTracer` so tick numbering is monotonic even after `drain_ticks()`. In `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:336-345`, `tick_index` is derived from `self.ticks.len()`, so draining the in-memory buffer causes later ticks to restart at 0. A long-running harness that periodically drains memory will therefore emit duplicate tick ids in its JSONL stream even though the simulation kept advancing. Keep a separate counter for the next tick id instead of tying ids to the retained buffer length.","rationale":"The bead positions the JSON-lines trace as a stable downstream artifact for long scenario runs and CI diffing. Duplicate tick ids make streamed traces ambiguous and break consumers that expect a single ordered timeline."},{"body":"Expand detail tracing beyond the current hard-coded pool subset. `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:154-220` snapshots only selected fields, but systems mutate other state that never appears in `pool_deltas`, for example `system:stability_tracker` updates `stability_tracker.instability_index` and the tracker baselines in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:96-123`, and `system:daily_shrimp` mutates reproductive state in `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:384-505`. At detail verbosity those stages can emit empty deltas even when they changed state, and `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:92-94` then silently reports `0.0` for absent pools. Either trace all mutation-relevant state or surface unsupported pools explicitly instead of treating 'untracked' as 'unchanged'.","rationale":"This is a direct contract miss for the tracing bead: downstream probes cannot inspect per-system deltas for arbitrary pools if some real state changes are invisible to the tracer."},{"body":"Preserve emitted event details in the trace schema instead of collapsing them to a count. `SystemTraceEntry` stores only `events_generated: usize` in `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:61-68`, and the engine fills it from `event_log.len()` deltas in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:450-458` and `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:505-513`. For stages like `system:daily_biofilter_maturity`, which can emit both `BiofilmMaturityIncrease` and `CycleProgressing` in one pass (`crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:370-390`), the JSONL trace cannot tell downstream consumers which event(s) actually fired. Store the emitted event kind/message/causes in each trace entry, not just a count.","rationale":"The bead requires tracing to record generated events and to be directly reusable by later harness/probe work. A bare count forces consumers to scrape `event_log` separately or invent a second schema, which defeats that goal."}],"summary":"The worktree diff is empty, so I reviewed the committed tracing implementation in HEAD. I found three correctness/robustness gaps in the trace API/schema: tick ids reset after draining, detail tracing omits real state mutations, and event identity is lost. Tracing-focused tests pass, but a full `cargo test -p tank_core` is currently blocked by unrelated pre-existing `BudgetEntry` test compile errors in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`."}